    {
      "id": "9hpqo80",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Introduction"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "An electric circuit provides a closed conducting loop necessary for continuous flow of electric current.",
        "In a series circuit, current remains identical across all components, while the total voltage is divided.",
        "In a parallel circuit, voltage across all branches remains equal, while the total current is divided.",
        "Safety devices such as fuses and MCBs protect circuit components against excessive current and short circuits.",
        "Ammeters are connected in series due to low resistance, whereas voltmeters are connected in parallel due to high resistance."
      ],
      "id": "v6b1jyy"
    },
